Package: SIMP
Title: Symplectic Integrators for Monte-Carlo Proposals
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R:
    person("Gilles", "Colling", , "gilles.colling051@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Author: Gilles Colling [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Gilles Colling <gilles.colling051@gmail.com>
Description: Symplectic integration of Hamiltonian systems and the Hamiltonian
    Monte Carlo proposals built on them. Explicit splitting schemes for
    separable Hamiltonians cover leapfrog, a two-stage minimum-error member
    tuned to cancel the leading energy error on a Gaussian target, and the
    Yoshida order 4, 6, and 8 members generated from a single triple-jump
    composition, so the whole family shares one stepper and one coefficient
    source. A generalized (implicit) leapfrog handles non-separable
    Hamiltonians, as in Riemannian dynamics with a position-dependent mass. The
    steppers are a header-only, scalar-templated C++ core that other packages
    can link against, so they run under automatic differentiation as well as
    plain double precision.
